<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>watermelon-pgp</id>
    <version>@VERSION@</version>
    <title>WatermelonPGP</title>
    <authors>Abul Tarannum</authors>
    <owners>tarannum22</owners>
    <summary>Self-hosted OpenPGP key management and folder encryption jobs, with a web UI.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[watermelon-pgp manages OpenPGP keys for your partners and encrypts or decrypts the files that land in watched folders, such as an SFTP server's upload folders. One program with a web UI, a command line and a Windows service.

This package installs `watermelonpgp.exe` into `C:\Program Files\WatermelonPGP` and puts that folder on the Path. It doesn't create a database or install the service: run `watermelonpgp init` and `watermelonpgp service install` yourself, as described in [the Windows Server guide](https://github.com/@REPO@/blob/v@VERSION@/docs/deployment.md#windows-server).

`choco upgrade` stops a running watermelonpgp service, replaces the program and starts the service again. `choco uninstall` refuses while a service runs the program (`watermelonpgp service uninstall` first) and never removes data directories or master keys.

Licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0, at your option.]]></description>
